% =========================================================
% ABSTRACT
% =========================================================
\begin{abstract}

YouTube has turned into a significant medium for public discussion whereby users give their views, feedback, acknowledgments, criticism and emotions through comments. Ubiquity of comments and their informal character make the human analysis impossible. Natural Language Processing provides techniques that help to process and analyze the textual information automatically.

The project demonstrates the implementation of an NLP framework for the analysis of YouTube comments written in English and Hinglish or containing code-mixed words and phrases. Hinglish refers to the informal use of Hindi and English within one comment, which has become a typical feature of Indian social media discourse. The workflow of the analysis encompasses different stages, such as the collection and cleaning of the dataset, the normalization of text, the tokenization and removal of stop words, the extraction of the features, sentiment analysis, and visualization.

The analysis is based on a large-scale dataset containing more than 20,000 YouTube comments. \cite{go,kouloumpis} The comments represent different forms of user reaction and can serve as a good example of how noisy user-generated social media text looks like. Thus, the project focuses on the development of a systematic pipeline for processing and analyzing such comments.

The study exemplifies the use of NLP techniques in multilingual and code-mixed posting on social media and sets a solid base for its further expansion with the help of machine learning and modern-language models.

\end{abstract}

