% =========================================================
% 1. INTRODUCTION
% =========================================================
\section{Introduction}

Social media is growing at a fast pace, leading to an increase in user-generated writing. YouTube is one of the most common video-sharing websites, allowing comments and engaging with the audience. Comments left by viewers provide various data regarding what people think, feel, and express about the content. \cite{go,kouloumpis}

It is not easy to examine the comments since there are a lot of comments on the famous videos on YouTube. Natural Language Processing (NLP) provides means for machines to comprehend human speech and analyse huge volumes of text. \cite{jurafsky,bird}

Sentiment analysis is one of the applications of NLP. It aims at determining the polarity of the text, which can be categorised as positive, negative, or neutral. Emotional analysis is a further development of sentiment analysis, where emotions that are present in the text can be determined. \cite{pang,liu}

Code-mixed language is a challenging aspect of Indian social media. A code-mixed text is one that contains many English and Hindi words. \cite{barman} For instance, a user may write:

\begin{quote}
``This video bahut achha hai, loved it!''
\end{quote}

The text consists of both English and Hindi expressions, which are typically referred to as Hinglish or Hindi-English mixed texts. Thus, the focal aspect of this project is to create an NLP methodology for analysing YouTube comments which contain both English and Hinglish phrases.

% =========================================================
% 2. PROBLEM DEFINITION
% =========================================================
\section{Problem Definition}

Comments on YouTube can be in a range of forms and are often not very formal. There can exist various forms of writing and visual expression like different spellings, symbols, repetitions, and expressions of emotions in the comments. Such a variety offers difficulties for computer analysis.

The problem which is tackled in this project is described below:

\begin{quote}
\textit{How can Natural Language Processing techniques be used to preprocess and analyse a large collection of YouTube comments containing English and Hinglish expressions in order to identify sentiment and emotional characteristics?}
\end{quote}

The proposed system aims to transform raw comments into a structured textual representation suitable for sentiment and emotion analysis.

