% 9. STOP-WORD PROCESSING
% =========================================================
\section{Stop-Word Processing}

The term "stop words" refers to words that appear often. The problem with using stop words in natural-language-processing is that they imply low discrimination for some tasks. Examples of stop words are the words "the," "is," "a," and "and," which are very common in the English language. \cite{bird,jurafsky} 

By using stop words in natural-language-processing, it is possible to help in reducing the number of dimensions in features. However, for the tasks of sentiment analysis, it is necessary to do this with care because some words should not be considered as stop words, as they can change the meaning of the statement. \cite{jurafsky,pang}

When dealing with Hinglish comments, it is often the case that regular stop-word lists are useless. Therefore, it is very important to take into consideration the nature of code-mixing in the text being analyzed.

