\section{Feature Extraction}

The raw text cannot be handled directly by machine learning algorithms. Therefore, text data needs to be converted into numerical form before processing them. \cite{manning,salton}

Various methods are available for extraction of the features from the data: \cite{manning,salton}

\begin{itemize}
\item Bag of Words
\item TF-IDF
\item Unigram features
\item Bigram features
\item Word-level features
\item Character-level features
\end{itemize}

\subsection{TF-IDF}

The term frequency inverse document frequency (TF-IDF) is one of the most popular ways of quantifying text data. \cite{manning,salton}

The inverse document frequency of the term may, in general, be defined as:

\begin{equation}
IDF(t) =
\log\left(\frac{N}{df(t)}\right)
\end{equation}


