where $N$ refers to the total quantity of documents, while $df(t)$ is the number of documents that include term $t$. \cite{manning,salton}

Thus, TF-IDF representation is defined as follows:

\begin{equation}
TFIDF(t,d)
=
TF(t,d)\times IDF(t)
\end{equation}

This representation gives higher importance to words that are relevant to a particular comment while reducing the influence of words that occur throughout the complete dataset. \cite{manning,salton} \cite{manning,salton}

